1
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:03,080
What is this?

2
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:07,720
A peace offering.

3
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,440
What do you mean?

4
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,730
The white flag of surrender raised by the other side.

5
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:17,240
How dare he fake illness to trick me.

6
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:21,240
But considering he took the initiative to make peace,

7
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,520
I'll reluctantly forgive him.

8
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:26,960
It seems you've got the primary and secondary conflicts

9
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:28,160
mixed up.

10
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:30,760
What?

11
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,360
The reason you were angry before

12
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,280
was jealousy, not faking illness,

13
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,080
right?

14
00:01:40,120 --> 00:01:42,880
This doesn't count as jealousy.

15
00:01:44,759 --> 00:01:46,400
I just can't stand seeing his pathetic face

16
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,930
when he flatters my sister.

17
00:01:49,039 --> 00:01:50,720
But now I know the reason.

18
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:51,960
Then

19
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:53,560
just forgive him.

20
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,440
For what reason?

21
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,280
Why are you still reading manga at your age?

22
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:07,080
Only boring adults would think that way.

23
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:09,280
My ex used to say the same thing.

24
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:12,080
It made it so I couldn't even read it openly.

25
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:14,400
But before today,

26
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,810
you never read it in front of me either.

27
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:19,360
Right. In the past,

28
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,840
I read it secretly.

29
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:24,079
However, you've passed my best friend test.

30
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:28,200
From today on, I'm going to read it freely in front of you,

31
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:31,040
until the end of the world.

32
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:34,760
When did I pass?

33
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,090
I don't know.

34
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,680
Actually, many things

35
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:40,360
happen imperceptibly and then burst out.

36
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,200
Is that from this manga too?

37
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:46,440
Let me see.

38
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,040
It's good, right?

39
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,000
Is it?

40
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,400
This big-nosed moon.

41
00:02:58,960 --> 00:02:59,760
What's wrong?

42
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,760
Don't you think a friend who randomly distances herself from you,

43
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,840
and then tricks you

44
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,480
into getting a shot because you faked an illness

45
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,680
is going a bit too far?

46
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:10,200
Such a long, thick needle.

47
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,080
Is it that hard to admit you like her?

48
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,240
To tell you the truth,

49
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:18,240
I've tailored a

50
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,480
cruel revenge plan just for her.

51
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,280
Is it that hard to answer my question directly?

52
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:25,000
I'm going to give her a taste of her own medicine.

53
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,040
These next few days,

54
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,880
I'll give her the cold shoulder

55
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:31,280
so she knows what it feels like to be treated hot and cold.

56
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,360
Deliberately distancing yourself

57
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,200
to test your place in her heart.

58
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,079
Nonsense.

59
00:03:35,079 --> 00:03:36,400
Spot on.

60
00:03:37,079 --> 00:03:38,280
It's just you and me here.

61
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,720
No third person will know

62
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,200
that you like Li Xinyue.

63
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,360
What?

64
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:45,600
You like Li Xinyue?

65
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,320
I...

66
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,410
Why are you here?

67
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,079
I've been here the whole time.

68
00:03:49,079 --> 00:03:50,840
You two were so engrossed in your chat,

69
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,040
so I didn't interrupt.

70
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:55,200
We absolutely can't let a fourth person know.

71
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,280
Why does this sound so familiar?

72
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:58,560
Don't worry, you two.

73
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,000
My lips are sealed.

74
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:05,440
Sister Yiying.

75
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,000
I have an explosive secret.

76
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,000
That Zhang Yang,

77
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,440
he likes...

78
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:10,240
I know.

79
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:13,860
Aren't you surprised?

80
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,279
Why can't I feel the joy

81
00:04:16,279 --> 00:04:18,959
of sharing gossip with you?

82
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,000
Look.

83
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,680
Zhang Yang, Tang Yi, Sister Yiying, Lin Yiyi.

84
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,720
I know.

85
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:27,160
Should I just tell Li Xinyue directly?

86
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,600
Are you stupid? She already knows.

87
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:33,600
Here you go.

88
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,000
The Cai family's ancient residential complex

89
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:40,080
was built by Cai Qichang, an overseas Chinese in the Philippines.

90
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,440
It was mainly built by Cai Zishen and his son.

91
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,960
Construction started with land purchase in 1855

92
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,400
and was completed in 1911.

93
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:50,680
It eventually formed this entire residential complex before your eyes,

94
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,000
known as the 'Little Forbidden City of Southern Fujian'

95
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,320
and the 'Grand View Garden of Southern Fujian Architecture'.

96
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:57,400
This is the whole building complex.

97
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:57,960
Stop.

98
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:03,880
Don't think you can just read the script because your Mandarin is standard.

99
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,140
It gives me a headache.

100
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:12,280
Is it wrong to speak standard Mandarin?

101
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:13,800
Of course not.

102
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,340
You are not arguing with me today.

103
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:19,610
Your happiness is the most important.

104
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:22,760
What's going on?

105
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:23,560
Zhang Yang.

106
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,530
I was wrong about what happened last time.

107
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:28,740
I apologize to you.

108
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:30,320
Li Xinyue.

109
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:32,640
It is work time now.

110
00:05:35,159 --> 00:05:35,960
Okay.

111
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,040
This skydiving is so thrilling.

112
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,280
Just watching it is awesome.

113
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,159
You're just watching.

114
00:05:50,159 --> 00:05:51,560
Would you actually dare to go?

115
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,560
If you don't do exciting things when you're young,

116
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:56,120
it'll be so boring when you're too old for it.

117
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:03,560
Kids these days are little terrors.

118
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:04,800
Who is it?

119
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,000
Our little client.

120
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:07,480
Probably a rebellious phase.

121
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,340
That's normal.

122
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,960
Kids at this age,

123
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:11,680
the more serious you act, the more annoyed she gets.

124
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,680
You need to do something special.

125
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,280
Something special?

126
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:18,920
For example?

127
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:22,040
Like taking her to do something thrilling.

128
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,640
Thrilling?

129
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,200
According to statistics,

130
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,880
seeking high-intensity sensory stimulation.

131
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,440
It is most common in adolescence and early adulthood.

132
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,480
This is part of their psychological development

133
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,200
and their search for self-identity.

134
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,400
Stop talking nonsense.

135
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,280
Well said.

136
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,240
Go on.

137
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:36,680
When they are 13 or 14 years old,

138
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,280
they like things that look dangerous,

139
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,159
exciting, and fun.

140
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,960
Can you stop coming up with bad ideas?

141
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,440
Good idea.

142
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:46,640
Dangerous and fun,

143
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,920
and exciting.

144
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,800
I think.

145
00:06:53,480 --> 00:06:54,600
I got it.

146
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:57,320
No way.

147
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,040
Yang,

148
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,200
welcome to Qingjing Taoyuan.

149
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:01,880
Look,

150
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:04,280
we have a lot of thrilling activities here.

151
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:05,210
Thrilling, huh?

152
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:05,980
Over there,

153
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:09,480
there's a 98-meter glass skywalk.

154
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:10,560
And here, look.

155
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,160
Warrior roller coaster.

156
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,480
Mongolian archery.

157
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:16,170
How about it? Anything you're interested in?

158
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,080
I don't think she's interested at all.

159
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:19,760
Why don't we choose something

160
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:21,560
a bit more approachable?

161
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,280
Who said I'm not interested?

162
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,680
How is it?

163
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,280
It looks good, right?

164
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,880
It's a great spot for taking photos.

165
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,280
Let me take a picture for you.

166
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:34,960
We have professional photographers.

167
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,290
They take great photos.

168
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:37,720
Photographer!

169
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:41,840
Photographer!

170
00:07:46,159 --> 00:07:48,640
It's okay, I'll take it with my phone.

171
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:50,360
Phone cameras are pretty good too.

172
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:53,080
You are very noisy. Let me be alone for a while,

173
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:53,880
okay?

174
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:55,880
Okay.

175
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,480
If you need anything later,

176
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,640
contact me anytime.

177
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,680
I will keep my line open.

178
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,560
Zhang Yang.

179
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,840
Don't you feel that when you run,

180
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,600
the bridge is moving?

181
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,200
Mr. Zhang.

182
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:15,880
Well, not only are you afraid of the dark,

183
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:17,760
you are also afraid of heights, right?

184
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:18,480
No.

185
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:22,040
The weather is nice today.

186
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:25,280
The weather is quite good.

187
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:26,280
But,

188
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,280
are you afraid of all

189
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,480
the thrilling rides?

190
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,799
Do we have a grudge?

191
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,640
Being polite,

192
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,440
only talking about work,

193
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,440
never crossing the line,

194
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,039
following all your instructions.

195
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,240
How does that displease you?

196
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,620
Anyway, you did it on purpose.

197
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,560
You don't seem to like

198
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,040
being treated politely by me.

199
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,040
Why is that?

200
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:48,800
Then tell me

201
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,720
your reason for intentionally ignoring me.

202
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,040
I am wrongly accused, your honor.

203
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:54,570
I have always been diligent and hardworking.

204
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,480
It is just human nature.

205
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,240
How could it be on purpose?

206
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,960
Slow down.

207
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,080
You... you...

208
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:06,080
Have you ever seen 'Final Destination'?

209
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:07,360
There's a bridge exactly like this in it.

210
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:08,890
I have. It's fine, let's go.

211
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,280
Just move your legs.

212
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:14,520
Hurry up.

213
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
What I recommend most is this Warrior Roller Coaster.

214
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,640
It is currently the longest, highest,

215
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,360
and steepest tubular slide in Fujian Province.

216
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,280
How is it?

217
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,280
How about we choose something else?

218
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,000
Letting a kid sit there,

219
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,280
what if she cries?

220
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,480
Does she look scared to you?

221
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,560
No, what if she cries,

222
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,680
what do we do if we get a complaint?

223
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:38,400
She won't be scared.

224
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:40,080
You have to think, if she complains about us...

225
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,600
You like her, and she likes you.

226
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,080
Why are you arguing here?

227
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,160
Ready? We're about to start.

228
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,080
Ready, ready.

229
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,440
Ready.

230
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:52,720
Hurry. Hold on to me if you're scared later.

231
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,400
Really?

232
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,440
You won't be.

233
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,900
It's very slow. Look at it.

234
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:01,440
Come on, fasten your seatbelts.

235
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,040
It's fine.

236
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,000
How is it? Are you feeling happier?

237
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,020
I don't like traveling at all.

238
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,560
Why?

239
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,040
Slow down.

240
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:35,000
Hello. Can I pet him?

241
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:35,480
Sure.

242
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,480
What's his name?

243
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,540
His name is Doudou.

244
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,280
Doudou.

245
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,240
How old is he?

246
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:41,200
Two years old.

247
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,220
You are two years old, Doudou.

248
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,240
So cute.

249
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,040
Come, Doudou,

250
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:46,800
say goodbye to the sisters.

251
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,720
Bye-bye, Doudou.

252
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:49,610
Let's go.

253
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,760
It seems you really like small animals.

254
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:57,300
Liking them isn't necessarily a good thing.

255
00:10:58,480 --> 00:10:59,600
What do you mean?

256
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,000
Whenever something you like leaves you,

257
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,840
you will be very sad.

258
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,960
How do you know so much at such a young age?

259
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:12,680
I'm not young.

260
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,480
I don't think I'll live past 18.

261
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:21,680
I thought the same way when I was your age.

262
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,760
But when you grow up a little more,

263
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:27,760
and see more of the world,

264
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:29,520
you'll find out.

265
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,640
This world is quite interesting.

266
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:36,280
That's because you're in love.

267
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:45,560
But you're different from them.

268
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,240
You don't lecture me.

269
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,360
Can we be friends?

270
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:57,040
Of course. We are good friends now.
